<title>PORTUGAL: Details of Portugal's 1997 draft budget proposals.</title>
<headline>Details of Portugal's 1997 draft budget proposals.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following figures are included in the Portuguese government's draft 1997 budget proposals presented to opposition parties for discussion on Friday.</p>
<p>The draft forecasts a drop in the proportion of state spending in the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) to 28.7 percent from 29 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>REVENUE, SPENDING AND PUBLIC SECTOR COSTS AS PROPORTION OF GDP</p>
<p>						1996 F     1997 F</p>
<p> Current revenues			  41.9	 42.4</p>
<p> Current spending			  42.7	 41.7</p>
<p> Current balance			   -0.8	 0.7</p>
<p> Capital revenues			   3.3	 3.5</p>
<p> Capital spending			   6.8	 7.1</p>
<p> Capital balance			   -3.5	-3.6</p>
<p> Total revenue			     45.3	45.9</p>
<p> Total spending			    48.8	48.8</p>
<p> Balance (without interest)	     0.7	 1.5</p>
<p> Global balance			    -4.3	-2.9</p>
<p>NOTE: F = Forecast</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
